06050</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b11"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Handoko</surname><given-names>KB</given-names></name><name><surname>Souverein</surname><given-names>PC</given-names></name><name><surname>van Staa</surname><given-names>TP</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Risk of aplastic anemia in patients using antiepileptic drugs</article-title><source>Epilepsia</source><year>2006</year><volume>47</volume><fpage>1232</fpage><lpage>6</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16886988</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b12"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kwan</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Brodie</surname><given-names>MJ</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Neuropsychological effects of epilepsy and antiepileptic drugs</article-title><source>Lancet</source><year>2001</year><volume>357</volume><fpage>216</fpage><lpage>22</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11213111</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b13"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Ricard</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Martin</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Tournier</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>A case of Parkinsonian syndrome, cognitive impairment and hyperammonemia induced by divalproate sodium prescribed for bipolar disorder</article-title><source>Encephale</source><year>2005</year><volume>31</volume><fpage>98</fpage><lpage>101</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15971646</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b14"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Verrotti</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Trotta</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Morgese</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Valproate-induced hyperammonemic encephalopathy</article-title><source>Metab Brain Dis</source><year>2002</year><volume>17</volume><fpage>367</fpage><lpage>73</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12602513</pub-id></citation></ref></ref-list></back></article>